      "english_ref": 14,
      "combined_translation": "14-19"
    },
    {
      "verse": 20,
      "sanskrit": "शब्दः स्पर्शश्च रूपं च रसो गन्धस्तथैव च। पञ्चमं सर्गमित्याहुर्भौतिकं भूतचिन्तकाः॥२०॥",
      "english": "Sound, touch, form, taste, and smell are the five objects of the senses, covering all things. The Mind lives upon all the senses and their objects.",
      "bhavadeepa": null,
      "chapter": 310,
      "parva_name": "शान्तिपर्व",
